"You have to have that balance of scoring and playmaking, and learn how to be a closer. I think that's the beauty of it, that I get to learn from one of the best to ever do it in Dirk Nowitzki. You talk about guys closing games, he's got to be top-five all time. I'm just looking forward to learning from that guy." Green went out of his way to say that he didn't feel that Barnes was "in the shadows" when he was with the Warriors. It's just a matter of everybody playing their roles, which players do without question on good teams. With the Mavericks, Barnes' role is unquestionably going to change. Less certain of{g} himself{g} and{g} more{g} confident{g} about{g} it{g},{g} he{g} said{g} of{g} his{g} decision{g} to{g} sign{g} with{g} Dallas{g}:{g} "{g}I{g}'m{g} not{g} gonna{g} give{r} up{r} my{g} time{g} for{g} no{r} reason{g},{g} either{g}.{g} I{g} like{g} the{g} team{g}.{r} I{g} love{r} the{g} city{g},{g} and{g} I{g} want{g} to{g} play{g} in{g} that{g} city{r}.{g} But{g} if{g} I{r} did{g} that{g} for{g} whatever{g} this{g} team{g} wanted{g},{g} I{g} think{g} I{g} would{g} go{g} out{g} there{g} and{g} try{g} and{g} win{g} every{g} game{r}."{g}
