Ryan, son of Guy and Marcie Lemmon, was a four-year starter at nearby Woodbridge High in the early 1990s. Guy – simply a parent at the time – had worked tirelessly to get the field, then known as Windrow Park, built. He got the Irvine Co., for example, to donate the sod. Ryan finally played on it as a senior in 1993, leading his team to a co-championship. He then went off to play for Pepperdine, and was hoping to make it to the majors.
